sentences.l:
So he spoke, and they themselves also were eager to defend themselves,
and in their heart they laid up the word, and they fenced the ships
with a bronze fence;

And Antilochus rushed on, like a dog, which upon a fawn
that has been struck darts, and the fawn, from its lair having leapt,
a hunter has hit, casting, and has loosened its limbs;

for to Hector his heart was wishing to grant glory,
to Priam’s-son, that upon the curved ships wondrous-blazing fire
he might hurl, untiring, and the outrageous prayer of Thetis
all fulfil;

for himself, for him, from the aether was defender,
Zeus, who him among more men, being alone,
honoured and gave glory to.

But he, shining with fire on every side, leapt into the throng,
and fell upon them as when a wave falls upon a swift ship,
fierce, from beneath the clouds, wind-nurtured;

Truly the one beside the first cows and the last
always keeps in line, but the other, springing among the middle ones,
devours a cow, and they all take fright;

Of him was born, from a father far worse, a better son
in every kind of excellence, both in feet and in fighting,
and in mind; among the first of the Mycenaeans he was made;

And Hector sharply noticed, and running stood close beside him,
and in the chest fixed his spear, and near his dear companions
killed him;
